{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d401","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06eb9-f212-7283-9b75-ad2ced5e882d"},"sequence":2139,"recorded_at":1780531400004273,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d7aaf52d-f59b-4e18-a931-19c896b89f9b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d7aaf52d-f59b-4e18-a931-19c896b89f9b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d7aaf52d-f59b-4e18-a931-19c896b89f9b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"e7ba8cdf-fb66-4662-9882-6bfcb7260e05"},"task_id":"e7ba8cdf-fb66-4662-9882-6bfcb7260e05","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"e7ba8cdf-fb66-4662-9882-6bfcb7260e05","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-04\n-\n-### 2210 — Terminal backend registry rework: aliasing bypass closed, four unmeasured domains measured\n+## 2026-09-04\n+\n+### 2340 — Terminal manifest/probe/capability-evidence admission (leaf 2): mutant protocol caught a mis-targeted expiry test\n+\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-1zvmw7 on leaf-1 checkpoint `9481a20`. New: `internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go` (closed Manifest/Probe/Evidence schemas, 16-row capability registry, generation digest, rule 1–6 reconciliation, expiry, signature-verifier seam, operation gate, `Registry.AdmitProbe`); tests `manifest_test.go` (black-box, independent JCS/identity/RSA-signing recipe) + `manifest_pin_test.go` (white-box for parse-unreachable arms). Leaf-1 files touched only for a doc line and 3 added wire codes; no gate logic changed.\n+- MUTANT PROTOCOL CAUGHT A MIS-TARGETED TEST: the \"expired evidence\" case re-signed mutated evidence (new ID) without refreshing the probe's `evidence_ids`, so under the original code it failed at liveness first (right arm, wrong reason to trust), and under a neutered-liveness mutant it failed at the ID-set arm instead of admitting — the test passed for the wrong reason and the mutant survived. Fix: every evidence-mutating case now calls `finalizeProbeIDs` after re-signing (6 cases + platform case), so each refusal lands on its intended arm; the corrected liveness mutant is killed.\n+- DETERMINISTIC SIGNATURES DEDUP: RSA PKCS1v15 is deterministic per key+message, so a \"distinct extra evidence\" fixture built with identical fields was byte-identical and correctly deduplicated — the test was wrong, production right. Unreferenced-object case now varies a supplementary fact (`ui_absent`) to force distinct bytes; identical-duplicate acceptance is pinned white-box as the stated bound.\n+- REAL PRODUCTION BUG FOUND BY TEST: strict decoder returned nil (not empty) slices for `[]`, so `json.Marshal` re-encoded them as `null` and omit-self identity recomputation diverged on claim-free/evidence-free documents. Fixed with non-nil array initialization; pinned by the empty-tuple admission test.\n+- EVIDENCE: board outcome artifact `TASK-260830-1zvmw7_manifest-probe-evidence.md` — 12/12 mutants killed (each grep-confirmed present, compiling, red, reverted byte-identical), suite/vet/gofmt/tracecheck exit 0, package coverage 87.1%.\n+\n+### 2210 — Terminal backend registry rework: aliasing bypass closed, four unmeasured domains measured\n"}}}
