killed.\n+- DETERMINISTIC SIGNATURES DEDUP: RSA PKCS1v15 is deterministic per key+message, so a \"distinct extra evidence\" fixture built with identical fields was byte-identical and correctly deduplicated — the test was wrong, production right. Unreferenced-object case now varies a supplementary fact (`ui_absent`) to force distinct bytes; identical-duplicate acceptance is pinned white-box as the stated bound.\n+- REAL PRODUCTION BUG FOUND BY TEST: strict decoder returned nil (not empty) slices for `[]`, so `json.Marshal` re-encoded them as `null` and omit-self identity recomputation diverged on claim-free/evidence-free documents. Fixed with non-nil array initialization; pinned by the empty-tuple admission test.\n+- EVIDENCE: board outcome artifact `TASK-260830-1zvmw7_manifest-probe-evidence.md` — 12/12 mutants killed (each grep-confirmed present, compiling, red, reverted byte-identical), suite/vet/gofmt/tracecheck exit 0, package coverage 87.1%.\n+\n+### 2210 — Terminal backend registry rework: aliasing bypass closed, four unmeasured domains measured\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"LOGBOOK.md","added":11,"removed":3},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
