{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d625","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06eb9-f212-7283-9b75-ad2ced5e882d"},"sequence":2413,"recorded_at":1780531400004821,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d7aaf52d-f59b-4e18-a931-19c896b89f9b","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"d7aaf52d-f59b-4e18-a931-19c896b89f9b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d7aaf52d-f59b-4e18-a931-19c896b89f9b"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Work is handed off to review — `TASK-260830-1zvmw7` is `to-review`, checklist 10/10, with two task-scoped outcome artifacts attached. Nothing was committed; the change sits uncommitted in the working tree for the board to checkpoint into the Change Request.\n\nWhat was built (all in `internal/terminalbackend`, on leaf-1 checkpoint `9481a20`):\n\n- [manifest.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go) — closed `ParseManifest`/`ParseProbe`/`ParseEvidence` over a strict decoder, the 16-row §4.D capability registry enforced at parse, `GenerationDigest`, `Reconcile` (rules 1–6 in deterministic order, expiry as `observed_at <= now < expires_at`, attestation via a caller-supplied `SignatureVerifier` seam with nil failing closed), `CapabilitiesForOperation`/`CheckOperation`, and the registry-bound production entry point `(Registry).AdmitProbe`. Three new wire codes, all in the pinned catalog vocabulary.\n- [manifest_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/terminalbackend/manifest_test.go) (black-box, independent JCS/identity/RSA recipe) and [manifest_pin_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/terminalbackend/manifest_pin_test.go) (white-box for parse-unreachable arms). Leaf-1 files touched only for a doc line and the 3 added codes.\n\nMeasured evidence: full suite, vet, gofmt, `go build ./...`, catalog-currency check, and tracecheck all exit 0; package coverage 87.1%; 208 passing test lines; 12/12 mutants killed, each grep-confirmed present, compiling, red, and reverted byte-identical. The `go doc -all` surface was re-audited — no exported path reaches the built-in registration arrays, pinned by a no-aliasing test.\n\nTwo findings worth knowing: the mutant protocol caught a mis-targeted expiry test (evidence mutations weren't refreshing `evidence_ids`, so it failed at the wrong arm — fixed, then the corrected mutant killed); and testing found one real production bug (strict decoder returned nil for `[]`, breaking identity recomputation on empty lists — fixed). Both are in the logbook and outcome artifact. Stated bounds (split-facts refusal, availability non-gate, conditional §4.C dependencies owned by lifecycle, key-registry seam) are documented in the artifact, not claimed as proven.","reason":null}}
